From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: WORKSPACE: skip glibc-linked LLVM and Python toolchain registrations

Upstream registers `@llvm_toolchain_llvm` (glibc-linked clang from
toolchains_llvm) and a hermetic Python 3.10 (also glibc-targeted).
Both fail to execvp on Chimera's musl libc — wrong ld.so.

Skipping `llvm_register_toolchains()` lets bazel fall back to
local_config_cc + the system clang (musl-linked, Chimera default,
binary-compatible with the LLVM 21 sources scip-clang links).
Override .bazelrc's BAZEL_DO_NOT_DETECT_CPP_TOOLCHAIN at the
command line so detection actually runs.

Skipping `python_register_toolchains` + `pip_parse` is fine
because the only consumers of @python_deps are //tools py_binary
targets we don't build — //indexer:scip-clang has no Python deps.

diff --git a/WORKSPACE b/WORKSPACE
index 3917191..c2fa7c5 100644
--- a/WORKSPACE
+++ b/WORKSPACE
@@ -33,30 +33,36 @@ load("//:setup_llvm.bzl", "setup_llvm_toolchain")
 
 setup_llvm_toolchain(name = "llvm_toolchain")
 
-load("@rules_python//python:repositories.bzl", "py_repositories", "python_register_toolchains")
-load("@llvm_toolchain//:toolchains.bzl", "llvm_register_toolchains")
-
-llvm_register_toolchains()
-
-python_register_toolchains(
-    name = "python_3_10",
-    # Remove this once agents stop running tests as root
-    # https://github.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/issues/47943
-    ignore_root_user_error = True,
-    python_version = "3.10",
-)
+load("@rules_python//python:repositories.bzl", "py_repositories")
+
+# LOCAL PATCH (Chimera / musl): upstream calls
+# `llvm_register_toolchains()` which points bazel's cc toolchain
+# resolution at `@llvm_toolchain_llvm//bin/clang` — a glibc-linked
+# pre-built from the `toolchains_llvm` rule's download.  That
+# binary can't execvp on Chimera's musl libc (wrong dynamic
+# linker: /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 vs /lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1),
+# so cc actions fail with "required file not found" once bazel
+# tries to compile LLVM 21 source, boost, protobuf etc.
+#
+# Skipping the register call here falls back to bazel's
+# local_config_cc auto-detection, which picks up the system
+# clang (`/usr/bin/clang`, musl-linked, Chimera's default).  The
+# .bazelrc sets `BAZEL_DO_NOT_DETECT_CPP_TOOLCHAIN=1`; override
+# that on the command line so detection runs.  Chimera's clang
+# is 21.1.8 which is binary-compatible with the bundled LLVM 21
+# sources scip-clang links against.
+
+# LOCAL PATCH (Chimera / Python 3.13): upstream calls
+# `python_register_toolchains(...)` (downloads a glibc-targeted
+# Python that doesn't run on Chimera's musl) and then
+# `pip_parse(...)` (whose vendored pip is incompatible with
+# Python 3.13 — `pkgutil.ImpImporter` was removed).  The only
+# consumers of @python_deps are //tools py_binary targets we're
+# not building.  Keep py_repositories() for rules_python
+# internals; skip the hermetic interpreter + pip_parse entirely.
 
 py_repositories()
 
-load("@python_3_10//:defs.bzl", "interpreter")
-load("@rules_python//python:pip.bzl", "pip_parse")
-
-pip_parse(
-    name = "python_deps",
-    python_interpreter_target = interpreter,
-    requirements = "//tools:requirements_lock.txt",
-)
-
 load("//:setup_deps.bzl", "setup_dependencies")
 
 setup_dependencies()
